{"duration": 74.913, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "McCoy oils railroad engines, then builds a machine to feed oil without stopping.", "start": 0.08, "end": 4.544}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He works as a fireman and oiler at the Michigan Central Railroad.", "start": 4.764, "end": 8.152}, {"beat": 1, "text": "McCoy can find only that work in Michigan.", "start": 8.572, "end": 10.772}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Other automatic oilers have already been patented.", "start": 10.992, "end": 13.539}, {"beat": 1, "text": "McCoy does skilled work in a home machine shop in Ypsilanti.", "start": 13.759, "end": 16.948}, {"beat": 1, "text": "He keeps refining his devices.", "start": 17.168, "end": 18.929}, {"beat": 2, "text": "A safety valve releases steam when pressure rises past a set limit.", "start": 19.349, "end": 23.102}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Boilers without one can explode.", "start": 23.322, "end": 24.944}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Firemen or crew members tie down valves for extra power.", "start": 25.164, "end": 28.374}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Tying a valve down pushes pressure past the safe limit.", "start": 28.594, "end": 31.424}, {"beat": 3, "text": "In 1872, McCoy patents his automatic lubricator for locomotives and ships.", "start": 31.844, "end": 37.048}, {"beat": 3, "text": "He lacks the money to build lubricators in large numbers.", "start": 37.268, "end": 40.312}, {"beat": 3, "text": "So McCoy assigns or sells his patent rights.", "start": 40.532, "end": 43.002}, {"beat": 4, "text": "You see, it's like a water bottle in your bag, so you never stop.", "start": 43.422, "end": 46.628}, {"beat": 4, "text": "His lubricator feeds oil to steam engines automatically.", "start": 46.848, "end": 50.136}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Trains run faster and stop less for lubrication and maintenance.", "start": 50.356, "end": 53.958}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The real reason: his 1872 patent is an automatic lubricator.", "start": 54.378, "end": 58.727}, {"beat": 5, "text": "It oils the steam engines of locomotives and ships.", "start": 58.947, "end": 61.702}, {"beat": 5, "text": "By 1899, his lubricator runs on almost all North American railroads.", "start": 61.922, "end": 66.753}, {"beat": 6, "text": "But McCoy's 1872 patent is not a safety valve.", "start": 67.173, "end": 70.631}, {"beat": 6, "text": "And 'the real McCoy' comes from Scotland, not from McCoy.", "start": 70.851, "end": 73.793}], "words": [{"w": "McCoy", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.57, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "oils", "start": 0.645, "end": 0.97, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "railroad", "start": 1.045, "end": 1.395, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "engines,", "start": 1.445, "end": 2.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "then", "start": 2.245, "end": 2.395, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "builds", "start": 2.445, "end": 2.695, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "a", "start": 2.72, "end": 2.745, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "machine", "start": 2.77, "end": 3.17, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "to", "start": 3.22, "end": 3.295, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "feed", "start": 3.345, "end": 3.52, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "oil", "start": 3.57, "end": 3.82, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "without", "start": 3.845, "end": 4.045, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "stopping.", "start": 4.095, "end": 4.581, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "He", "start": 4.829, "end": 4.904, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "works", "start": 4.954, "end": 5.179, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "as", "start": 5.229, "end": 5.304, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "a", "start": 5.329, "end": 5.379, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "fireman", "start": 5.454, "end": 5.904, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "and", "start": 5.954, "end": 6.029, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "oiler", "start": 6.104, "end": 6.679, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "at", "start": 6.754, "end": 6.804, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "the", "start": 6.829, "end": 6.879, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Michigan", "start": 6.929, "end": 7.279, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Central"